      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// This code simulates a successful SELL order.\n// It also contains the real Dhan API call, commented out for future use.\n\n// Get data from the previous nodes. We need the Google Sheets data.\nconst tradeData = $('Get row(s) in sheet').item.json;\nconsole.log('--- Incoming Trade Data for SELL ---', tradeData);\n\n// =========================================================================\n// --- SECTION 1: REAL DHAN API CALL (Currently Commented Out) ---\n// =========================================================================\n/*\nconst accessToken = 'YOUR_DHAN_ACCESS_TOKEN';\nconst apiUrl = 'https://api.dhan.co/v2/orders';\n\nconst requestBody = {\n  securityId: 'YOUR_SECURITY_ID', // You'll need to get this ID\n  exchangeSegment: 'NSE_EQ',\n  transactionType: 'SELL', // The only change is here\n  quantity: tradeData.Quantity,\n  orderType: 'MARKET',\n  productType: 'INTRADAY',\n  price: 0\n};\n\nconst response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'access-token': accessToken,\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    'Accept': 'application/json'\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify(requestBody)\n});\n\nif (!response.ok) {\n  const errorData = await response.json();\n  throw new Error(`Dhan API Error: ${JSON.stringify(errorData)}`);\n}\nconst realApiResponse = await response.json();\nconsole.log('--- Real Dhan SELL Response ---', realApiResponse);\n*/\n// =========================================================================\n\n\n// =========================================================================\n// --- SECTION 2: MOCK API RESPONSE FOR TESTING (Currently Active) ---\n// =========================================================================\nconsole.log(`Simulating SELL order for ${tradeData.Quantity} shares of ${tradeData.Symbol}.`);\n\n// =========================================================================\n\n// --- MODIFICATION START ---\n// Get data from the immediate input node, which contains our 'reason' and 'pnl'.\nconst mergedInput = items[0].json;\n// --- MODIFICATION END ---\n\n\n// IMPORTANT: We must pass the row_number AND the new data to the next step\n// so we know which row to update in Google Sheets.\nconst outputData = {\n  row_number: $('Get row(s) in sheet').first().json.row_number,\n  status: 'SOLD',// <-- ADDED THIS LINE\n  pnl: $input.first().json.PnL        // <-- ADDED THIS LINE\n};\n\nconsole.log('--- Output to Next Node ---', outputData);\n\n// Return the data for the final step.\nreturn [{\n  json: outputData\n}];"
      },
